01:01:35.600 --> 01:01:40.880
And I posited that I think we only have two&nbsp;
sight lines. And this circles back to my early&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:40.880 --> 01:01:46.920
days with animation. And I said, "I've noticed&nbsp;
when I'm stealing that if I move in a straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:46.920 --> 01:01:52.000
line that there's a transition point from A&nbsp;
to B, that when something is no longer at A,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:55.760
that people expect to be there, they bounce back,&nbsp;
their attention bounces back like a rubber band&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:55.760 --> 01:02:03.240
to B. But if I move in a half circle from A&nbsp;
to B, when we get to that destination point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:03.240 --> 01:02:07.880
nobody ever looks back at the point of origin."&nbsp;
I said, "So I sense that there's two types of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:07.880 --> 01:02:12.320
sight lines and there's a kind of suppression&nbsp;
that happens during those. And I think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:12.320 --> 01:02:16.040
that's an interesting place to experiment with."
