called back to the mayor of Kyiv and they said&nbsp;
he hasn't been on a call. There's a future there&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:18.000 --> 02:05:22.120
that's coming that is intense. So a lot of&nbsp;
these concepts where I mentioned them from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:22.120 --> 02:05:28.040
pickpocketing and things, that's why I noticed I&nbsp;
didn't go to just getting a better money belt. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:28.040 --> 02:05:32.880
went to the importance for concepts. The&nbsp;
overconfidence will work against people.&nbsp;

02:05:32.880 --> 02:05:36.560
Tim Ferriss: Yeah. You see people in any major&nbsp;
city, we're sitting in New York City right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:36.560 --> 02:05:43.400
the number of people I have seen see a go&nbsp;
signal and walk across the street with earbuds&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:43.400 --> 02:05:52.040
in looking at their phones, not checking either&nbsp;
direction in this city is unbelievable. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:52.040 --> 02:05:55.160
hundreds of them. I've seen hundreds.
Apollo Robbins: Two times when I've been to Japan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:55.160 --> 02:06:01.080
the first time I went there, there was this kind&nbsp;
of connection of everybody around. Then the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:01.080 --> 02:06:06.400
time, a couple decades later I went back, the&nbsp;
latching in of the smartphones. It really does&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:06.400 --> 02:06:13.360
become this kind of, not narcissism, but this&nbsp;
kind of egocentricism of through their virtual&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:13.360 --> 02:06:18.200
world they're exploring out there. While they're&nbsp;
plugged into that, like the matrix I guess you'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:18.200 --> 02:06:24.360
say, their physical body becomes vulnerable.
So as a predator mindset of looking at people&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:24.360 --> 02:06:29.920
like that, there used to be a term among thieves&nbsp;
called the grift sense. They felt that the grift&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:29.920 --> 02:06:35.360
sense was more important than technique. The&nbsp;
ability to extract that from someone and be&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:35.360 --> 02:06:42.320
able to know where their attention was, how much&nbsp;
they're investing their attention on a thing. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:42.320 --> 02:06:46.680
it becomes more salient when somebody is holding&nbsp;
their phone and you can see where their attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:46.680 --> 02:06:50.440
is and you can see what they're doing.
Tim Ferriss: So I don't want to beat a&nbsp;&nbsp;

